{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1468693-tc-assasins-instead-aberrant-on-timeline","id":1468693,"title":"TC Assasins instead Aberrant on timeline","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-23T09:16:55-08:00","id":1468693,"title":"TC Assasins instead Aberrant on timeline","content":"With coming of <b>TC Anima</b> more and more I'm eager to make multi-era game with <b>Trinity Continuum</b>, with one story in each era. But I have a bit problem - I do not lika <b>Aberrant</b> as era concept - or rather playable setting. I do not like 'modern superhero' in my more or less 'hard s-f' <b>Trinity</b> gameline. So I want to erase <b>Aberrant</b> as playable era.<br /> <br /> In place of it, I want too put <b>TC </b><b>Assassins</b> I found very compelling. Assassins are rather dark, where <b>Aberrant</b> is rather light ( or seems as such) so I suspect this timeline changes will lead to some changes in <b>Anima</b> era then.<br /> <br /> To be clear - I WANT Aberrant War in game setting. I want this 3rd War World analogue in game. I can even have some rouge Novas to be found from time to time later on - just I do not want 'nice Nova Age' in my timeline.<br /> <br /> I suspect some assassins, with coming years, can become rouge Novas as with Flux manipulation - or that assassins will be first 'Aberrants Hunters'?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-03-2021, 04:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T18:05:43-08:00","id":1468714,"title":"","content":"To start with, I personally like the darker superheroes idea myself. It's a trope, I get it, and I appreciate it when I play it... but yeah, it comes across as even more high fantasy than LotR settings do for me. I personally liked the 1e take on Aberrants over the 2e for the same reason. It gave more than just lip service to the idea that supers would change the world in ways that are not all happy &amp; light.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1468693-tc-assasins-instead-aberrant-on-timeline#post1468693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not like 'modern superhero' in my more or less 'hard s-f' <b>Trinity</b> gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>&quot;Hard s-f&quot;</i>? Can I assume you're just ignoring the idea of Talents magically pulling what they want out of alternate universes as needed? Cos that explanation of their abilities strikes me as just as high fantasy as anything from the Aberrant timeline. Not arguing, it's just I (too?) personally ignore the 'psuedo-science' explanation for Talents and simply have them as being outstanding individuals - Inspiration, Dramatic Editing, etc being completely PLAYER concepts with no in-world explanation. Just like Momentum, a purely ludonarrative concept that has no in-world basis beyond something like <i>&quot;John Wick is just that awesome&quot;.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1468693-tc-assasins-instead-aberrant-on-timeline#post1468693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect some assassins, with coming years, can become rouge Novas as with Flux manipulation - or that assassins will be first 'Aberrants Hunters'?</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that the Assassins are Talents on steroids, using <i>Talent Flux</i>, not Novas affected by <i>Quantum Flux</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T05:28:44-08:00","id":1468831,"title":"","content":"Admittedly I am not following Anima\u2019s development and Kickstarter, but I echo the question: When was the Continuum have ever been hard SciFi?<br /> As for the actual topic of the thread:<br /> From an after the war perspective the legacy of the Nova age looks like this: (simplification)<ul><li>A group of people displays capability beyond what is possible for normal humans.</li> <li>This leads to a period of rapid social change and technological development, including the establisment of extrasolar colonies.</li> <li>Eventually, conflict breaks out between the above group and their followers and the rest of the populace.</li> <li>As a result of this conflict, large portions of the planet became uninhabitable, several key infrastructures get damaged/collapses, and millions die/go missing.</li> <li>The powered group gets forced off-world, the war results in loss of the technology that renders interstellar travel possible, amongst several other technologies that are no longer reproducible.</li> <li>There is a general paranoia that the war may restart, either from the return of the novas or normal people may erupt and restart the war.</li> </ul>So if we rip out the superhero aesthetic, the same can be done with more grounded transhumanist antagonists or Artificial intelligence like in Eclipse Phase. (Through probably softer singularity than the Titans were)<br /> The last point is the least ideal fit, but the spontaneous eruptions can be replaced with sleeper agents and transhumanists trying to replicate the original augmentation procedures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24185-zsarnok","name":"Zsarnok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T05:41:15-08:00","id":1468836,"title":"","content":"You know you can just take the 1E setting and then use the current rules if you want things grimdark. Or else just borrow ideas or else just tweak the entire thing. That is why they gave the Tones part of the Aberrant book. To let you make it the way you want it to be. Not to mention the very core conceit of the setting is, whatever you decide is canon. It is all part of a branching continuum. So, if you want to skip Aberrant, then you can. Just use Aeon, Anima, Adventure!, and Aether. You can just say that the events presented in the timeline of the post Aberrant War books is canon for your new timeline and skip over Aberrant completely.<br /> <br /> Although, I got to echo the thoughts of others...Trinity is not hard sci-fi. I mean, look at Aeon...grav crystals. People who can teleport on their own. Aliens who can shoot lasers out of their body. The Coalition. The fact that a lot of the events of Aeon has been due to sentient telepathic arrogant little puffs of plasma. Not really hard sci-fi unless you have done a lot of changes to the setting. And if you have, then keep right on doing it and adjust away. If you did make Trinity hard sci-fi, I honestly would love to see what you did to make it that way. I love hearing how people tweak their games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T18:20:22-08:00","id":1468879,"title":"","content":"I don't have Aberrant second edition yet, but is &quot;Cape&quot; really that hard coded into the setting? Project Utopia definitely pushed that angle of contextualizing Nova's in the 1st edition and it was something that the populace as a whole latched onto (at least in the US) but I didn't think it was something inherent to being a Nova. It was just one aesthetic and lifestyle you could choose among many. I imagine the Teragen also adopt &quot;codenames&quot; that could be seen as adopting super hero or villain identities, but it seems like it would be more about establishing a new identity outside of your baseline one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T19:16:00-08:00","id":1468883,"title":"","content":"TC:Ab actually takes pains to give the Storyguide as much options to take the setting to his or her liking. It wouldn't be hard to make a fairly small change to make, say, Transcendence and Transformations an even bigger hassle than it normally is, making Aberrant more like Deviant: the Renegades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T23:31:20-08:00","id":1468902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Planguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1468693-tc-assasins-instead-aberrant-on-timeline?p=1468879#post1468879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have Aberrant second edition yet, but is &quot;Cape&quot; really that hard coded into the setting? Project Utopia definitely pushed that angle of contextualizing Nova's in the 1st edition and it was something that the populace as a whole latched onto (at least in the US) but I didn't think it was something inherent to being a Nova. It was just one aesthetic and lifestyle you could choose among many. I imagine the Teragen also adopt &quot;codenames&quot; that could be seen as adopting super hero or villain identities, but it seems like it would be more about establishing a new identity outside of your baseline one.</div> </div> </div> </div>No its not. They still have all of the different roles Nova's play in society, Cape is just the one most publicized. Some of the NPCs are scientists, researchers, celebrity's and the like, and Elites offer a way to use your powers as a sanctioned superpowered merc.<br /> <br /> The Teregen as a whole doesn't use codenames instead taking a new name and discarding their human name as they consider themselves as no longer human or bound by human rules. Now this is in general, specific Teregen members may keep tier original names and identities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27184-darrendalca","name":"DarrenDalca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27184_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-26T01:26:22-08:00","id":1468908,"title":"","content":"Terragen don\u2019t have codenames, they have God names, once they are not human they don\u2019t have reason to stick to their human names. It\u2019s part of reinventing and overwhelming themselves. Utopia and Elites are more codename prone, to keep their real identities safe or for publicity reasons.<br /> <br /> But as it was said before, Novas as too diverse to be described as \u201cCapes\u201d, there are more than a few of those, but in general it\u2019s about what you can do and what you want to do, if your group what to deal with the impacts of hyper inventors and their inventions in society, you have a solid set to work with (even some rules you can use to predict the impact), if you want to deal with the social repercutiam, no problem, there are nova politicians (not only in the elected places, but also working form them). Now if you want to go full superhero, the most obvious Novas are those that act as superheroes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T01:32:26-08:00","id":1469472,"title":"","content":"The more I read about canon timeline implications in <b>Anima</b>, more I envision this 'darker' version of <b>Continuum</b>, the more I see that <b>Assasins</b> would hunt the newsent Novas, on government related assassinations contracts, Instead of building Project Utopia or Daedalus League, Novas would be powerful, good meaning, but only individuals - that are infiltrated by suspicions governments, wanting finally to take them out, afraid of their powers. In this timline variant, Novas = Aberrants from the start, at least to the general public. Analogy to Red Scare of 1950s America is good idea on this. Or at least how I see this.<br /> <br /> For example, instead of Project Utopia given special status in 2024 by United Nations from <b>Abberant</b>, in <b>Assasins</b> secret directive was signed by all <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Group_of_Ten_(economics)\" target=\"_blank\">G10 countries</a> to eliminate Novas. Day-to-day assassins' are contracted to take out those individuals.<br /> <br /> By 2040-50s, Novas are so hunted down, they rebel - and create <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brotherhood_of_Mutants\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of Mutants</a> similar society. By 2060s there is full blown Aberrant War.<br /> <br /> Think this version of Continuum would be much more cynical and darker, laying fundaments for truly fascists' FSA, for example.<br /> <br /> Much more rage and pain for both sides of the story...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-05-2022, 04:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T03:34:59-08:00","id":1469480,"title":"","content":"With permission from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24985_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24985\" data-vbnamecard=\"24985\">Mateus Luz</a> , I would incorporate those 'more cynical' takes for <b>Aberrant War</b> on this timeline. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1469121-support-for-an-aberrant-war-official-supplement?p=1469147#post1469147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see a book telling the story from the aberrant point of view, for example, the Directive triggering Wicoff explosion in a tentative if put him down, or the Novas trying to to take control of Olympus as the only place they could avoid persecution (people end up starving not because of the Novas themselves, but because the governments stop supplying Olympus after the amovas took control of it).<br /> <br /> It would be an awesome counterpoint to the \u00c6on narrative of the war.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T07:54:12-08:00","id":1469731,"title":"","content":"Stealing some ideas on Assasins in Aberrant eras from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24955-waldi\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24955\" data-vbnamecard=\"24955\">Waldi</a> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Waldi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1469259-trinity-continuum-assassins-pre-order?p=1469713#post1469713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds good - especially since similar things would also be very logical with other Allegiances. With some Allegiances in other eras, the whole thing is even clearer. I would be very surprised, for example, if De Vries in Aberrant or Norca un Aeon had no connections to the shadow.<br /> <br /> My take on assassins in the Aberrant era would be that the whole basic situation is still comparatively similar to that in the present - with two differences: &quot;The Signal&quot; specialises more and more in eliminating novas that are dangerous for Baseline people - they mutate into &quot;The Boys&quot;, so to speak. In the process, they have entered into alliances of convenience with the Directive on more than one occasion.<br /> The Swarm, on the other hand, has dropped to the status of a minor society thanks to internal disputes and financial problems. In exchange, De Vries is now part of the Council.<br /> <br /> In Aeon, I would find it quite interesting if an Assassin society was a secret militant arm of ISRA. This highly dangerous and surprisingly fanatical group uses precognition to determine what kind of people could endanger humanity in the future and then has them eliminated before they can do any harm.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T08:22:39-08:00","id":1469736,"title":"","content":"Feel free to do so <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24955-waldi","name":"Waldi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T08:47:51-08:00","id":1469739,"title":"","content":"I personally don\u2019t see why the \u201cmood\u201d would impact the timeline, I mean, by aberrant war the general population was feeling largely oppressed by Novas, what means a more cynical/dark aspect of reality.<br /> <br /> Sure, adding Assassins to the timeline will have some impact, but it is not a big deal, as most of the contracts don\u2019t have a bug impact Day Light (they kill people, but not the big ones). Assassins may kill some Aberrants, but even them have limitations that Novas don\u2019t. I means, I would be happy to get a mastery that raise the Assassin scale a few scales, but it would be largely momentaneous while novas are permanently in that scale. Sure there will be Assassins killing Novas, but they would not get that many Novas down, you need tanks and ships, or maybe a Goku or 2, and I don\u2019t think it\u2019s the way Assassins are going.<br /> <br /> Now, a raise in Shadow, and by that I mean Assassins being the big bad guys causing WWIII (a war with no Aberrants, by the way), is another thing. It could go all the way to Anima existence, replacing Aberrant war by a big conventional war lead by the societies of shadow (not openly lead, just making their war reach day light using their contacts).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T08:29:49-08:00","id":1470634,"title":"","content":"Idea on what I want to base a story - Assassins got the List of targets to get on - or that each previous target points to another. At the end of List/conspiracy is Aberrant - maybe even Divus Mal himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T08:05:27-08:00","id":1470712,"title":"","content":"Some ideas from quotes from <b>TC Assassins</b> about crossovers with main <b>TC Core</b> setting - to extrapolate more for the alternate <b>TC</b> timeline...<br /> <br /> <b>The Allegiances and the World of Shadow </b><br /> <i><b>Trinity Continuum Core Rulebook</b> details several Allegiances, beginning on p. 160. The majority of these Allegiances are assumed to operate in Daylight, but some brush against Shadow. <b>9</b> and <b>Archangel</b> have ties to Twilight, as they frequently deal with or hire underworld elements. Similarly, <b>Pharaoh\u2019s Lightkeepers</b> have plenty of reasons to dabble in Twilight activity. Rumor holds that the <b>\u00c6on Society</b> has connections directly within the <b>Daughters of the Jacobins</b>, and that the <b>Global Cartography Initiative</b> has provided the <b>Signal</b> with valuable technology every now and then. On more than one occasion, the <b>Neptune Foundation</b> has thought they were saving the day, only to discover they\u2019d walked directly into an ongoing Shadow plot. <b>Les Fantomes</b> operates almost exclusively in Twilight and on more than one occasion has received mysterious help from a member of Shadow.<br /> Using the Allegiances makes for a different set of obstacles or allies who are not Shadow\u2019s usual fare of brutal killers, corrupt politicians, or morally bankrupt business people. This also opens the door to crossover play between Talents and Assassins. </i><br /> <br /> <b>Assassins and Super Science </b><br /> (...)<br /> <i>The <b>Transcendent Alliance</b> (<b>TC Core Rulebook</b>, p. 190) has dispatched eccentric Inspired inventors to reach out to willing Societies in order to exchange their technological prowess in return for vast sums of money from Shadow.</i><br /> <br /> (<i><b>Daughters of the Jacobins</b></i> write-up) <b>The \u00c6on Society Connection </b><br /> <i>The Daughters maintain a network of allies beyond the Shadow. Since its earliest days, members of the \u00c6on Society have been aware of the Daughters of the Jacobins, supporting their ideals or directing them against dangerous enemies the \u00c6on Society could not act against. Legend says that the elderly Isidora Legrand turned Mercer down on his offer to join the organization, but the two have always been connected, if not at a distance. The Society helped the Daughters with their investments in the \u201840s, and on occasion, the Daughters assist them to this day. Assassins disdain the meddlesome behavior of the \u00c6on Society, but the Daughters firmly protect their alliance. Improbably, they claim Henri Legrand left a letter promising that the \u00c6on Society would be essential to achieving their ideals, a prediction made over a century before the Society\u2019s founding. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-20-2022, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T13:07:54-08:00","id":1470730,"title":"","content":"Now, thinking more about the plot - I think it could be Aeon Group modern ( 2020s) that hire Assassins ( probably from Daughters of Jacobians) to take out more and more problematic Aeon ex-founding member - Dr. Primoris, a. k. a Davis Mal now! \ud83d\ude32","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-17-2022, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T13:09:36-08:00","id":1470731,"title":"","content":"(Double post <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-18-2021, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-20T18:19:50-07:00","id":1479203,"title":"","content":"Okay, what events I would need to change to make 'Novas were in secret hunted down by Assassins - but Aberrant War finally broke free'?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-20T18:29:14-07:00","id":1479204,"title":"","content":"Revert to something more like Aberrant 1e, with the Assassins replacing Project Proteus as the people who see Novas as a threat to humanity and are hunting them down. <br /> <br /> It really doesn't take much of a change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-21T00:25:13-07:00","id":1479217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1468693-tc-assasins-instead-aberrant-on-timeline?p=1479204#post1479204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Revert to something more like Aberrant 1e, with the Assassins replacing Project Proteus as the people who see Novas as a threat to humanity and are hunting them down.<br /> <br /> It really doesn't take much of a change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should Aeon Society then be mixed in this actions? Aeon in 2020s is still not very convinced in 'innocent' of Novas? Remember - it's alternate timeline, we did not have space station burning starting canonical Aberrant Era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T00:15:42-07:00","id":1479329,"title":"","content":"It depends on how and when \u00c6on learned about the appearance of novas. The official history assumes that the Galatea Event was as big as it was because anything smaller wouldn't have cracked the Doyen Barrier and the world would have continued to be populated by stalwarts and mesmerists instead of novas and psiads (and then only in the wake of less extreme Events). <br /> <br /> Perhaps in this timeline, Sara and Michael worked together on duplicating the Hammersmith Event, and their combined efforts resulted in a shared Quantum and Psi booster Event. Like a matter/antimatter reaction, where both the matter and antimatter cancel each other out but tremendous energy is released in the process, maybe the combination of Quantum and Psi energies being released together caused most of both energies to \u201ccancel out\u201d for the purpose of triggering Novas and Psis, but effectively magnified each other's effects for the purpose of breaking the Doyen Barrier. <br /> <br /> And perhaps it also effectively supercharges the Flux output, resulting in daredevils becoming a permanent thing instead of fading away over the decades, and significantly increasing the population of Assassins. <br /> <br /> That is, it becomes more of a Flux Event, with the side effect of upgrading stalwarts and mesmerists to novas and psiads. <br /> <br /> I'd be inclined <i>not</i> to have \u00c6on behind the hunting of the Aberrants; reserve that for the Assassin allegiances. Likewise, none of the Aberrant factions appear in this timeline; instead, use the factions from the core book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T02:15:34-07:00","id":1489075,"title":"","content":"For this Timeline change a bit Project Utopia? \ud83e\udd14 Something much more darker or in hiding to public? Or just left the Project Proteus in existence - without Utopia? Remember, I want to make Novas very new thing in 2025 - and in hidden at this time. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24985_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24985\" data-vbnamecard=\"24985\">Mateus Luz</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24955-waldi\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24955\" data-vbnamecard=\"24955\">Waldi</a> - some thoughts?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Project_Utopia\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Project_Utopia</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Project_Proteus\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Project_Proteus</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-04-2022, 05:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T07:00:55-07:00","id":1489107,"title":"","content":"More thinking about timeline - Maybe I simply<b> made </b><b><i>Project Proteus</i> as secret United Nations Security Council branch</b> that is 'controlling' new Nova 'threat' ( from POV of baselines ). Then <b>Proteus </b>is open to hire various Assassins Societies on newly coming up Novas - <u>without</u> telling Assassins they hunt superhumans in reality? \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-04-2022, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T13:38:37-07:00","id":1493353,"title":"","content":"So I'm finally hammering my alternative Trinity Timeline for this variant...<br /> <br /> <b>2018</b> - We DID NOT get Galatea explosion. History to this day run as in real world.<br /> <br /> <b>2019-2021</b> - Pandemic of COVID19.<br /> <br /> <b>2022-2024</b> - Russia-Ukraine war. Russian Federation lost. Ukraine is accessing to European Union and NATO. War ended on May 9th, on <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Victory_Day_(9_May)\" target=\"_blank\">Russian Victory Day</a>, greatest Federation national holiday. Russia humiliated starts process that will end de facto annexed into China, in coming decades. ( by the time of <b>Anima</b> era. )<br /> <br /> <b>2025</b> - <b><i>T</i></b><i><b>okyo Incident.</b></i> ( Maybe on May 9th anniversary, to be symbolic? ) Variant of N-Day where Davis Mal <i>did <b>not</b></i> broke Doyen Barrier - only made 'holes' in it. Novas start to show up, but are much, much less populate than in canon <b>Aberrant </b>era.<br /> <br /> <b>June of 2025</b> - <b>United Nations Security Council</b> secretly start <b><i>Project Proteus</i></b> - Assassins network that are ( unknowingly ) send to kill this few Novas that Erupted.<br /> <br /> <b>Rest of timeline events are just like in canon Continuum</b> - minus 'Novas superheroes and splendor'. From time to time lonely Nova try to be a good guy - but they are often literally hunted by <b><i>Project Proteus</i></b>. It still ends in <b><i>Aberrant Wars</i></b> as we know them from canon.<br /> <br /> <b>Sum up of Timeline variant</b> - Basically, we will have S-F thriller instead of canon <b>Aberrant</b> Era - in what Novas are strictly pointed and called as Aberrants from start - not many 'positive Novas' in this timeline. <hr /><br /> Bonus is that we can fix some things with canon timeline - like how <b>OpNet </b>in this version is full virtual reality network, sending senses across, straight with GLASS implant of <b>Anima</b> era - not just '10G' data network in canon <b>Aberrant </b>era. \ud83d\ude0e<br /> <br /> <b>OpNet</b> is developed here in 2040s, but as Novas are very distrusted and <b>Aberrant Wars</b> started in 2056 - network do not have time to propagate. Instead, in this variant timeline, OpNet is introduced to whole world in times of Great Reconstructions after Wars, in 2070s. GLASS implant is making this network full virtual senses reality network from start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-20-2022, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-30T05:02:11-07:00","id":1495878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1468693-tc-assasins-instead-aberrant-on-timeline?p=1469472#post1469472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The more I read about canon timeline implications in <b>Anima</b>, more I envision this 'darker' version of <b>Continuum</b>, the more I see that <b>Assasins</b> would hunt the newsent Novas, on government related assassinations contracts, Instead of building Project Utopia or Daedalus League, Novas would be powerful, good meaning, but only individuals - that are infiltrated by suspicions governments, wanting finally to take them out, afraid of their powers. In this timline variant, Novas = Aberrants from the start, at least to the general public. Analogy to Red Scare of 1950s America is good idea on this. Or at least how I see this.<br /> <br /> For example, instead of Project Utopia given special status in 2024 by United Nations from <b>Abberant</b>, in <b>Assasins</b> secret directive was signed by all <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Group_of_Ten_(economics)\" target=\"_blank\">G10 countries</a> to eliminate Novas. Day-to-day assassins' are contracted to take out those individuals.<br /> <br /> By 2040-50s, Novas are so hunted down, they rebel - and create <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brotherhood_of_Mutants\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of Mutants</a> similar society. By 2060s there is full blown Aberrant War.<br /> <br /> Think this version of Continuum would be much more cynical and darker, laying fundaments for truly fascists' FSA, for example.<br /> <br /> Much more rage and pain for both sides of the story...</div> </div> </div> </div>Now this is probably the actual reaction governments would have to something like this: contain and eliminate. Humans would not go quietly into the good night. It's why we rule the earth now. Well said I may revamp my time line and story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27624-logansrun68","name":"logansrun68","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-02T09:24:59-08:00","id":1498622,"title":"","content":"With finally getting TC <b>Aeon</b> 2E corebook from sale, I can finally finalise my <b>Wyrd\u2019s Darker Trinity Timeline</b>. I use here a lot of timeline quotes from <b>Anima </b>and <b>Aeon</b> books, for fuller look on events.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Wyrd\u2019s Darker Trinity Timeline</b></span></i><br /> <br /> <b>Up to 2025</b> - History run as in real world ( beside <b>Trinity</b> shenanigans )<br /> <br /> <b>2018</b> - We DID NOT get <b>Galatea Explosion</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>2019-2022</b> - Pandemic of COVID19.<br /> <br /> <b>2022-2024</b> - Russia-Ukraine war. In the end, Russian Federation lost. Ukraine is accessing to European Union and NATO. War ended on May 9th, on <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Victory_Day_(9_May)\" target=\"_blank\">Russian Victory Day</a>, greatest Federation national holiday. Russia humiliation starts process that will end de facto annexed into China, in coming decades. ( By the time of <b>Anima</b> era. )<br /> <br /> <b>2025,</b> <b>May 1st</b> - <b><i>Tokyo Incident.</i></b> Variant of <b>N-Day </b>where Davis Mal <i>did <b>not</b></i> broke Doyen Barrier - only made 'holes' in it. Novas start to show up, but are much, much less populate than in canon <b>Aberrant </b>era.<br /> <br /> <b>June of 2025</b> - <b>United Nations Security Council</b> secretly start <b><i>Project Proteus</i></b> - Assassins network across their Societies, that are ( unknowingly ) send to kill this few Novas that already Erupted.<br /> <br /> <b>2030s - 2050s</b> - <b>Nova Age?</b> They start in hiding, unsure of their powers and hunted by <b>Proteus</b>. In year 2030, first Novas are proud enough to stand in the light and talk with media and their outcast family, without maniacal laugh \u2013 <b>Queer Nova Alliance</b>. On the other hand, from the <b><i>Tokyo Incident</i></b> forward, antisocial superhumans are pointed as<b><i> Aberrants </i></b>by governments agencies, like <b>9</b> or <b>Alert Status 1 </b>( See <b>Trinity Continuum Core Rulebook</b> ) Term leaks to press in few cases, living from now on it\u2019s own in Internet.<br /> <br /> In those decades, Earth is divided on subject of Novas. Some points their humanity, under all the powers. Individuals invent hyperfusion and superconducting batteries, giving humanity unlimited cheap energy in some instances \u2013 but it\u2019s always not enough. Even with reversing global climate change projects and famous \u2018blooming Sahara Desert\u2019 \u2013 worst enemies were other Novas, more \u2018criminally minded\u2019. And there are also baselines humans pointing not every superhuman is knight in the shining armour. There are those that steal and kill others simply cause they can. There are those taken by Davis Mal the Teragen movement. And there were simply Nova psychopats \u2013 those become Aberrants.<br /> <br /> During the height of this time, some of superhumans built research bases on several asteroids and planets within the solar system and explored the stars. China\u2019s controlled Nova led an exploration team to <b><i>Khantze Lu Ge </i></b>in 2040 and founded several other extrasolar colonies. In addition, several groups of humans paid space-traveling Novas to help them establish colonies on habitable extrasolar planets. A few of these colonies were founded in secret and records of most others were lost during the <b>Internet Crash</b> in <b>2067</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>No wonders of Nova Age?</b> <hr /><br /> So with <b><i>Tokyo Incident </i></b>and creation of <b><i>Project Proteus</i></b> in 2025, did Nova Age really started before Aberrant Wars? Yes and no. With tumultuous times and society divided on Novas subject, some of them reached the heights of canonical <b>Trinity Continuum</b>. But also they were hindered by they more malice inducing brethren. Many project of official Nova Age were devised in this timeline, also, but most of the time were not so widespread and much more individual projects \u2013 until baseline humanity took those techs in their own hands. Particular example is <b>OpNet</b>. <hr /><br /> <b>No OpNet\u2026 yet</b> <hr /><br /> In this variant timeline, <b>Great Crash</b> of <b>2067</b> destroys <i><u><b>Internet</b></u></i> \u2013 10G to be precise \u2013 not <b>OpNet</b>. The later in this version is Nova tech developed in <b>2049</b>, and beside great speeds and uniform laying ( that 10G also had ) <b>OpNet</b> let to send full senses across it. <i>True virtual environment immersive simulation!</i> But as it was Novas invention \u2013 it was very distrusted outside of superhumans supports and cults. When <b>Aberrant Wars</b> started in <b>2056 </b>- network do not have time to propagate around the world. Instead, in this variant timeline, <b>OpNet</b> is introduced to whole world in times of Great Reconstructions after Wars, in 2070s <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">\u2013 of course, \u2018Aberrant protected\u2019 in Gen 2 of tech</span>. <b>GLASS implant</b> is making this network full virtual senses experience from start, hyping and propagating around the planet and Sol system. <hr /><br /> <b>2025 - 2105 </b>\u2014 <b><i>Japan</i> </b> \u2014 After <i><b>Tokyo Incident </b></i>in <b>2025</b>, Japan close it\u2019s borders for few months. In coming years, Japan becomes more and more isolation. Rumors say that Novas started there and government is exterminating with their sources. <b>In 2053</b>, Japan finally closes its borders and changes its name to match the one it uses internally \u2014 <b>Nippon</b>. <b>Until 2105</b>, no outsiders are allowed to step onto Nihonjin soil, and all contact with the outside world comes through the large offshore floating settlement of Makaro-Shima.<br /> <br /> <b>2079</b> \u2014 In response to declining Church membership and empty parishes resulting from the Urban Schism, the papal bull <b><i>Qua dispensatione animam</i></b> (\u201cThe Dispensation of Souls\u201d) from Pope Innocent XV states that transubstantiation can occur via digital projection. So long as the sensation of consuming bread and wine are experienced by a real priest, any Catholic sharing that sensory experience may enjoy communion with God and receive transmission of the sacrament over <b>OpNet</b>. The Anglican and Orthodox Churches follow suit, as do other denominations of Christianity. At the same time, the pope elevates <b>Friar</b> <b>Byrne Draper</b> to bishop and sets him to lead the ecclesiastical province of <i><b>Cascade </b></i>in once Canada, with the expansive mandate to hold Mass for worldwide audiences projecting into the city\u2019s municipal servers.<br /> <br /> Rest of events in this timeline is the same as in the official canonical timeline. \ud83d\ude0e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-17-2023, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T00:26:41-08:00","id":1504817,"title":"","content":"In the future of eras Aberrant , Assassins and Aeon and beyond...<br /> <br /> Russia clears its hackers of any legal accusations! \ud83d\ude32 Hackers are totally free in Russia to do what they want! \ud83d\ude32<b